<!--
    Adaptive icon foreground: the Konecta N mark, drawn as vector geometry
    taken from konecta.svg rather than traced from the 200x200 JPEG, so it
    stays sharp at every density and has real transparency.

    Placement maths (computed from the actual path bounds, not eyeballed):

      * The N glyph occupies x 46.339..87.273, y 4.694..29.422 in SVG space,
        so 40.934 x 24.728 units, an aspect ratio of 1.655.
      * Scaled by 1.368056 it becomes 56.00 x 33.83 units inside the 108x108
        viewport - comfortably within the 72x72 safe zone that survives every
        launcher mask shape, and with roughly the same breathing room as the
        supplied square logo.
      * The outer group then centres it exactly on (54, 54).

    The inner group reproduces the per-path translate() from the SVG, since
    VectorDrawable has no per-path transform attribute.

    This drawable is also used as the <monochrome> layer for Android 13 themed
    icons, where the system ignores fillColor and uses only the alpha.
-->
